}
```

The doc comment does document it, and behavior is correct (verified: dedupe semantics are byte-identical to the pre-refactor inline block). But the call site — `if (tokens && !isFaSegmentReplay(tracking, tokens)) appendUsageSample(...)` — reads as a stateless check; a future reader reordering or double-calling it would silently change dedupe behavior. A name that carries the side effect (`registerFaSegment`, `markFaSegmentSeen`) or moving the "seen" write next to `appendUsageSample` would make the contract obvious. Pure naming/structure polish — no behavior change requested.
"}

